{"id":"0f1ed56f-87a0-4a8a-b834-d730c17144a2","revision":0,"last_node_id":14,"last_link_id":11,"nodes":[{"id":10,"type":"Note","pos":[400,-470],"size":[700,370],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"8.0.1","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["Muse MOSS Sheet Designer - example\n\n1. Pick your model files in the three loaders (FLUX.2 Klein 9B shown; Qwen Image 2.1, Flux3 Klein and MOSS-Image also work - see README).\n2. Load a character reference image (image 1). Optional: connect a second LoadImage to detail_image, or a Muse 5-panel pose sheet to pose_image.\n3. Describe the character / outfit / body in the text boxes (or press Describe with an LC Vision Loader on vision_model). Nude-only details go in nsfw_details. Shoes go in the designer's Footwear part prompt, not in outfit.\n4. Choose views in the designer cards. Portrait + Front + Left side + Right side + Back fills the template output.\n5. Press Next view or All views. Each view appears in its card; nothing is output yet.\n6. Per card: Confirm good views, New seed, Show prompt to edit it, or Apply edit. Only that view re-renders.\n7. Press Build final sheet now - the sheet and template go to the Save nodes.\n\nPrompt list: pick a list in the preset dropdown, then press Prompt list. Images/captions go to the dataset output.\nKlein: steps 4, cfg 1. Qwen 2.1: 20-25 steps, or 8 with turbo/Lightning."],"widgets_values_named":{"text":"Muse MOSS Sheet Designer - example\n\n1. Pick your model files in the three loaders (FLUX.2 Klein 9B shown; Qwen Image 2.1, Flux3 Klein and MOSS-Image also work - see README).\n2. Load a character reference image (image 1). Optional: connect a second LoadImage to detail_image, or a Muse 5-panel pose sheet to pose_image.\n3. Describe the character / outfit / body in the text boxes (or press Describe with an LC Vision Loader on vision_model). Nude-only details go in nsfw_details. Shoes go in